comments.message:
This can be really confusing to have two events. If really needed I would prefer just one which actually indicates a "reset". 

https://www.dmtf.org/sites/default/files/standards/documents/DSP2065_2025.3.pdf has PlatformReset but unfortunately, it just has one arg `string: The type of reset that occurred.` -- no mention of what.

@paligill@gmail.com I noticed that all the Platform 1.3.1 message registry spec just assumes there is a "computer system" and does not really support multi-host systems or have the message registry provide the resource name/path etc.
